# /vendor/etc/init/gsi_defaults.rc: fallback property default for a GSI on the
# DM63 and DW100U-silver watches (same file for both). Rationale and the [I]
# marks: devices/VENDOR_GSI_PATCH.md, "GSI defaults".
# Read by init from /vendor/etc/init (Android 10+ parses that directory).
# ro.config.low_ram is not here: build properties load before early-init, it is
# written into /vendor/build.prop by scripts/vendor_gsi_patch.sh.
# Not set on purpose: any ro.lmk.* property (lmkd autodetects), and the app
# freezer (no property of ours controls it, see the doc).

on early-init
    # VNDK version fallback. The GSI's vndk-detect (post-fs, before rw-system.sh)
    # overwrites this with the version it finds in the vendor sepolicy; this value
    # is what rw-system.sh sees only if that detection finds nothing. The watches
    # report no ro.vndk.version.
    setprop persist.sys.vndk 27
